// The one place the UI talks to the server. Types come from the Rust side
// (generated by `cargo test`), so a changed contract fails the type check.
//
// Traps: `getProvider` waits for a store on its way (`storing`, `store`), so the settings' line and the page
// "Advanced" each show what the other stored; a preset put in use is such a store. A lorebook's editor asks of
// one of the library or of a card's own alike (`LoreOf`, `lorePath`); an entry's reference is one part of the
// address (`entryPath`). `getAccount` and `renameAccount` are for ../account.ts alone, which
// keeps the account for the screens. The page calls itself by a mark of its own (`PAGE`), sent with every
// request and in the event socket's address, so it is not told of its own changes. While the server waits for
// the password, every asking but `getLock` and `unlock` is answered 423 (`isLocked`). A page that is to sign
// in (another device's without a session, or one whose session ended: a 401 with `SIGN_IN`) starts anew, and
// main.ts shows the sign-in screen. The companion's settings are changed by `changeCompanion` alone. A backup is saved by a form's post into a hidden frame (`saveBackup`).
